# Code owners for suculent/thinx-device-api.
#
# There is one maintainer today, so the global rule would be enough on its own.
# The path rules below exist to keep the sensitive surfaces explicitly owned as
# collaborators are added, and to make review of those paths a deliberate act
# rather than an accident of who happened to open the PR.
#
# This file assigns reviewers; by itself it blocks nothing. It only gates merges
# once branch protection on main turns on "Require review from Code Owners" —
# which, with a single owner, would block every merge, because GitHub does not
# let you approve your own pull request. Enable that rule only after a second
# reviewer with write access exists.

*                           @suculent

# CI/CD: anything that can publish an image, deploy, or mint a token
/.circleci/                 @suculent
/.github/                   @suculent
/.githooks/                 @suculent
/Dockerfile                 @suculent
/Dockerfile.test            @suculent

# Dependency surface
/package.json               @suculent
/package-lock.json          @suculent
/.snyk                      @suculent

# Authentication, session handling and request middleware
/lib/middleware/            @suculent
/lib/router.*.js            @suculent
/lib/thinx/oauth-github.js  @suculent
/lib/thinx/oauth_return.js  @suculent
/lib/thinx/origins.js       @suculent

# Runtime configuration and deployment topology
/conf/                      @suculent
/services/                  @suculent
